Description: antinomie: leave the recorder's symbols out of /proc/kallsyms and wchan
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-21

/proc/kallsyms lists every kernel symbol by name to any user (only the addresses are hidden without privilege): 365 of them were the recorder's (ant_send, ant_monitor_*, the debug engine, their initcall and export entries) and some 300 more were its static functions and data under generic names. /proc/<pid>/wchan shows a waiting task's function by name, so a task parked by the debug engine showed one of its functions.  The recorder's objects are now bracketed: section_begin.o, linked first in kernel/antinomie, and section_end.o, linked last, put a label at the start and the end of each section the directory puts symbols in (.text, .rodata, .data, .bss and the per-CPU area). The linker keeps one directory's input sections of a kind together and in link order, so each pair encloses exactly its symbols. ant_symbol_hidden() answers for an address in one of these ranges or for a name the recorder gives its hooks elsewhere (ant_*, and __pfx_ant_*, __ksymtab_ant_*, __setup_ant_* and initcall entries made from it). /proc/kallsyms skips those lines and wchan shows 0 for them, as for a running task. The early parameter handler of bootstrap.c is renamed after the recorder (ant_boot_gpa_param) so its init symbols are named like the others.  Nothing else changes: the kernel's own symbol table is complete, so stack traces, %pS, kprobes, kallsyms_lookup_name() and the debugger keep every name. Root can still find the recorder (/proc/kcore, a kprobe by name, a /proc/<pid>/stack): that is inspecting the guest kernel, not reading a listing.

---
diff --git a/fs/proc/base.c b/fs/proc/base.c
index 704cf6a06..cea11a1fc 100644
--- a/fs/proc/base.c
+++ b/fs/proc/base.c
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@
 #include <linux/cn_proc.h>
 #include <linux/ksm.h>
 #include <uapi/linux/lsm.h>
+#include <linux/antinomie_stealth.h>
 #include <trace/events/oom.h>
 #include "internal.h"
 #include "fd.h"
@@ -428,7 +429,8 @@ static int proc_pid_wchan(struct seq_file *m, struct pid_namespace *ns,
 		goto print0;
 
 	wchan = get_wchan(task);
-	if (wchan && !lookup_symbol_name(wchan, symname)) {
+	if (wchan && !lookup_symbol_name(wchan, symname) &&
+	    !ant_symbol_hidden(wchan, symname)) {
 		seq_puts(m, symname);
 		return 0;
 	}
diff --git a/include/linux/antinomie_stealth.h b/include/linux/antinomie_stealth.h
index a691b5cbe..3601e71fb 100644
--- a/include/linux/antinomie_stealth.h
+++ b/include/linux/antinomie_stealth.h
@@ -7,7 +7,14 @@
 /* Architecture setup, before the command line is first printed: take the
  * host's antinomie_* options out of it and apply them. */
 void ant_cmdline_take(char *cmdline);
+/* Whether a program reading symbols by name (/proc/kallsyms, wchan) must not
+ * see this one: the recorder's own. name may be NULL. */
+bool ant_symbol_hidden(unsigned long address, const char *name);
 #else
 static inline void ant_cmdline_take(char *cmdline) { }
+static inline bool ant_symbol_hidden(unsigned long address, const char *name)
+{
+	return false;
+}
 #endif
 #endif
